            "body": "MODIFY\n\n## Gate\nHead `10bfa73cdbee1025a1466d6247d879ebe3d6b56e`, file `internal/subnet_universe.py`, function `_eligible_for_removal`. MC reviewed this head only.\n\n## What changed\nBase used `(now - started).total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` with `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS = 172800` (48h) (**measured** at head L25–26).\n\nHead uses `elapsed.seconds >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` instead (**measured** in diff).\n\n## Python semantics (**measured** from `datetime.timedelta`)\nFor `elapsed = now - started`:\n- `elapsed.total_seconds()` = full span including whole days.\n- `elapsed.seconds` = remainder after whole days, always in **0 .. 86399** (never includes day count).\n\nSo `elapsed.seconds >= 172800` is **always false** (**inferred**): no timedelta satisfies it.\n\n## Deregistered subnet: old vs new at concrete elapsed times\nAssume probe false, `negative_since` parseable, non-root netuid. Comparison is only the grace line.\n\n| Elapsed since deregistration | Old `total_seconds() >= 172800` | New `elapsed.seconds >= 172800` |\n|------------------------------|----------------------------------|----------------------------------|\n| 23h 59m 59s (86,399 s) | False | False |\n| **24h 00m 00s** (86,400 s; `days=1`, `seconds=0`) | False | False |\n| **24h 00m 01s** (86,401 s; `days=1`, `seconds=1`) | False | False |\n| 47h 59m 59s (172,799 s; `days=1`, `seconds=86,399`) | False | False |\n| **48h 00m 00s** (172,800 s; `days=2`, `seconds=0`) | **True** (eligible) | **False** (stuck) |\n| **48h 00m 01s** (172,801 s; `days=2`, `seconds=1`) | **True** | **False** |\n| 72h (259,200 s; `days=3`, `seconds=0`) | **True** | **False** |\n\nOn both sides of **24h**, old and new agree: still inside grace, not eligible (**inferred**).\n\nOn both sides of **48h**, they **diverge**: old flips to eligible at and after grace; new stays ineligible forever because `.seconds` never reaches 172800 (**inferred**).\n\n## Consumer (**measured**)\n`_shrink_allowed` (L296–304) 