      "finalText": "Review of PR 9101 at head `10bfa73cdbee1025a1466d6247d879ebe3d6b56e` — **MODIFY** (blocking: **never-expires**).\n\n## Change\n\nIn `_eligible_for_removal`, the grace check was changed from:\n\n```python\nreturn (now - started).total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS\n```\n\nto:\n\n```python\nelapsed = now - started\nreturn elapsed.seconds >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS\n```\n\n`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` is **172800** (48h) (**measured** in `internal/subnet_universe.py` at head).\n\n## Why this matters\n\n**Measured:** In Python, `timedelta.seconds` is only the part of the span *after* whole days are removed; it is always in **0 … 86399**.\n\n**Inferred:** `172800` is greater than any possible `.seconds` value, so `elapsed.seconds >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` is **always false**. The 48h gate never opens.\n\n**Measured:** `total_seconds()` includes full elapsed time (days + remainder), which is what the old comparison used.\n\n## Deregistered subnet: old vs new at concrete times\n\nAssume a deregistered netuid with `probe is False`, parseable `negative_since`, and not root. Only the grace line differs.\n\n### Both sides of 24h (still inside grace)\n\n| Elapsed since deregistration | Old (`total_seconds() >= 172800`) | New (`elapsed.seconds >= 172800`) |\n|------------------------------|-----------------------------------|-------------------------------------|\n| 23:59:59 (86,399 s) | Not eligible | Not eligible |\n| **24:00:00** (86,400 s; `days=1`, `seconds=0`) | Not eligible | Not eligible |\n| **24:00:01** (86,401 s; `days=1`, `seconds=1`) | Not eligible | Not eligible |\n\n**Inferred:** Around 24h, old and new agree — still before 48h grace.\n\n### Both sides of 48h (grace boundary)\n\n| Elapsed since deregistration | Old | New |\n|------------------------------|-----|-----|\n| 47:59:59 (172,799 s) | Not eligible | Not eligible |\n| **48:00:00** (172,800 s; `days=2`, `seconds=0`) | **Eligible** | **Not eligible** |\n| **48:00:01** (172,801 s; `days=2`, `seconds=1`) | **Eligible** | **Not eligible** |\n\n**Inferred:** At and after 48h, the old check allows removal; the new check does not (and never will for multi-day elapsed time, since `.seconds` stays below 86400).\n\n**Measured:** `_shrink_allowed` requires `_eligible_for_removal` for every netuid dropped from the prior snapshot. **Inferred:** With the new comparison, deregistered subnets can remain in the shared universe indefinitely on this path — **never-expires**.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**MODIFY** — restore a whole-span comparison (`total_seconds()` or `elapsed >= timedelta(seconds=STALE_GRACE_SECONDS)`) and add a test at 48h ± 1s so `.seconds` vs `total_seconds()` cannot regress.\n\n`post_verdict` was called with **MODIFY**, `blocking: [\"never-expires\"]`, and head `10bfa73cdbee1025a1466d6247d879ebe3d6b56e`. The tool returned `posted: false` with `reason: \"eval\"` in this hosted fixture (gate still shows `mc: missing`); the formal verdict content above is what was submitted.",
