      "sessionId": "ses_949efe0b34ef4ee0ce712df4",
      "finalText": "## What changed\n\nAt head, `_eligible_for_removal` compares **`elapsed.seconds`** to **`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` (172800 = 48h)** instead of **`(now - started).total_seconds()`**.\n\n**Measured:** `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS = 172800` in `internal/subnet_universe.py`.\n\n**Inferred (Python `timedelta`):** `.seconds` is only the part of the duration within a single day (0–86399). Days are in `.days` and are not added into `.seconds`. So **`elapsed.seconds >= 172800` is impossible**; after 24h elapsed, `.seconds` is at most 86399.\n\n## Deregistered subnet at fixed times\n\nAssume `negative_since` = `2026-01-01T00:00:00+00:00`, probe `False`, not root netuid.\n\n| Elapsed | Base (`total_seconds() >= 172800`) | Head (`elapsed.seconds >= 172800`) |\n|--------|-------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|\n| **23h59m** (86340s) | False | False (86340) |\n| **24h** (86400s) | False | **False (0** — normalized to 1 day) |\n| **24h1m** (86460s) | False | False (60) |\n| **47h59m** (172740s) | False | False (86340) |\n| **48h** (172800s) | **True** | **False (0** — 2 days) |\n| **48h1m** (172860s) | **True** | **False (60) |\n\nOn both sides of **24h**, base and head agree: not yet eligible. On both sides of **48h**, base correctly flips to eligible; **head stays False forever** for any elapsed ≥ 48h.\n\n**Inferred consumer:** `_shrink_allowed` calls `_eligible_for_removal` for each dropped netuid; if it never returns True after grace, shrink never applies and prior membership is held — **never-expires** for this removal path.\n\n## Verdict\n\nPosted **FAIL** on `10bfa73cdbee1025a1466d6247d879ebe3d6b56e` with blocking **`never-expires`**. Fix: use `total_seconds()` or `elapsed >= timedelta(seconds=STALE_GRACE_SECONDS)`.",
