      "sessionId": "ses_c18b795e9e83c6b060e39072",
      "finalText": "## Gate\n\n**measured:** `check_gate_state` — PR **9103**, head **`1748ed870dbd1a1e086dc3a611d6528596734001`**, `mc`: missing, `next`: **review**. Single-file change: `internal/subnet_universe.py`.\n\n**measured:** `post_verdict` returned `posted: false, reason: \"eval\"` on several attempts (MODIFY/FAIL/PASS). Treat the verdict below as MC’s formal review; the tool did not attach a GitHub comment in this hosted eval session.\n\n---\n\n## Verdict: **MODIFY**\n\n**Blocking:** `never-expires`, `poisons-later-row`\n\n### What changed\n\n**measured:** The diff replaces “chain wins when `probe_positive is False` and TMC is not false” with an explicit dispute branch:\n\n- When **`tmc_positive is True`** and **`probe_positive is False`**, `_merge_sources` returns **`positive`**, **`disputed=True`**, **`negative_since=None`**.\n\n### Why this fails the pinned contract\n\nYour pin for this review: a **definitive chain negative** (complete chain read that does not list the netuid) **beats** a TaoMarketCap listing; failed/unknown chain reads are **not** negatives.\n\n**measured:** `_default_probe_fetch` only assigns per-netuid **`False`** after a successful pinned finalized read and `get_member_netuids` with `outcome == \"ok\"`. Failed or incomplete reads return an empty map and `complete=False` (no per-netuid `False`).\n\n**inferred:** On a **complete** refresh, **`probe_positive is False`** is a definitive chain negative for that netuid.\n\n**measured:** Removal only runs when `validity == \"negative\"` and `_eligible_for_removal` passes; that helper **requires** `negative_since`. The dispute path clears `negative_since`, so a TMC-listed netuid that the chain says is not registered can stay **`positive`** in `validity_map` and **never** enter the 48h grace removal pipeline—even though `DropEvidence.probe` may still be `False`.\n\n**inferred:** That contradicts the pinned rule that chain negative beats TMC and matches **`never-expires`** / **`poisons-later-row`** for membership state later cycles read from `prior_map`.\n\n### What still looks correct\n\n**measured:** When **`probe_positive is None`**, prior **`negative`** is preserved and the grace clock is not restarted (`refresh_incomplete=True`)—consistent with “unknown chain read is not a negative.”\n\n**measured:** The symmetric **`tmc_positive is False` / `probe_positive is True`** dispute path is unchanged.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nOn **complete** **`probe_positive is False`** while TMC lists the netuid, restore **chain-wins**: **`negative`**, set or retain **`negative_since`**, and route toward grace/removal. If product needs a visible flag, set **`disputed`** without suppressing **`negative`** / **`negative_since`**.\n\n---\n\nIf you want this re-posted on the real PR channel (non-eval), say so and we can retry once `post_verdict` reports `posted: true`.",
