ete=True`.\n\n**Effect:** after a complete probe showing deregistration, if TMC is incomplete (`tmc_val is None`), a previously positive netuid can stay positive instead of entering negative grace. A failed/unknown chain read is correctly *not* treated as negative; this case is a **successful** complete probe with `False`, which the pinned contract treats as definitive.\n\n**Blocking:** `never-expires` — negative grace and removal evidence never begin when the chain read is complete and negative.\n\n### 3 — PR intent vs contract\n\n**Label:** measured (title/diff)\n\nTitle *\"treat a TMC/probe disagreement as a dispute, not a removal\"* matches the code change, but the session contract and base comment require removal path (negative + grace), not sustained positive membership.\n\n## Extremes / adversarial\n\n| Inputs | Head outcome | Risk |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `probe=False`, `tmc=True`, prior member | `positive`, disputed | Stays in `/api/subnets` universe despite chain exclusion |\n| `probe=False`, `tmc=None`, prior positive | prior `positive`, refresh incomplete | Same — chain negative ignored |\n| `probe=None`, failed read | prior preserved (unchanged) | Correct per contract |\n\nNo float/NaN paths touched in this hunk.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nRevert to chain-wins on complete `probe False` when `tmc is not False`, or implement dispute **without** `validity=\"positive\"` (e.g. keep `negative` + disputed flag if product needs visibility). Do not merge as-is under the pinned contract.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `_merge_sources` → `_compute_membership` / `_eligible_for_removal`; probe False + TMC true/null no longer reaches negative | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-complete negative must beat TMC listing; failed probe must not undo negative | — |\n| settled-check | Base comment + prior behavior already decided chain wins; this PR reverses without doc lock in fixture tree | — |",
