      "finalText": "## Verdict: **FAIL** (posted for head `1748ed870dbd1a1e086dc3a611d6528596734001`)\n\nReview is subnet-review-gate on PR **9103** (*universe: treat a TMC/probe disagreement as a dispute, not a removal*).\n\n### What changed\n\n**Measured:** The PR replaces the branch that treated any complete chain negative with TMC not explicitly false (`probe False`, `tmc True` or `None`) as **`negative`** + **`negative_since`** with a narrower rule: only **`tmc True` + `probe False`** → **`positive`**, **`disputed`**, no grace clock.\n\n### Why this fails the pinned contract\n\n1. **Chain negative vs TMC listing** — **Measured** on head vs base in `_merge_sources`; **inferred** through `_compute_membership` / `_eligible_for_removal`. A complete registration read that omits the netuid (`probe=False`) while TaoMarketCap still lists it (`tmc=True`) used to enter the removal path (negative + 48h grace). On this head it stays **`positive`**, so the subnet never leaves the shared universe for that reason alone. That contradicts: *a definitive chain negative beats a TaoMarketCap listing.*\n\n2. **`probe False` + incomplete TMC** — **Measured** control-flow change. Base forced **negative**; head falls through and can **keep prior positive** when `tmc=None`. A **failed** chain read still must not count as negative; here the probe is **complete** and **False**, which under your contract is definitive.\n\n**Blocking tags:** `poisons-later-row`, `never-expires`.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nRestore chain-wins on complete `probe False` when `tmc is not False`, or if “dispute” is required for UX, do not represent that as `validity=\"positive\"` without starting negative/grace semantics consistent with the contract.\n\nFormal comment is on the PR via `post_verdict`. Gate fixture still shows `next: review`; in production the channel should pick up the FAIL and move to **blocked** until the head changes.",
