t T0.\n\n## Cycle 2 (chain read still failing) at three fixed times — inferred\nAssume cycle 1 already ran at T0 with this code (clocks anchored at T0). Each cycle 2 run: same failed probe (`{}`, incomplete); `probe_val=False` again; `negative_since` stays T0 (not reset).\n\n| Time | Elapsed vs T0 | `_eligible_for_removal` | What cycle 2 does |\n|------|----------------|-------------------------|-------------------|\n| **T0 + 47h59m59s** | 172799s < 172800 | false | Keeps prior **netuids**; entries stay `negative` with `negative_since=T0`; no drops; degraded / incomplete refresh. Membership count unchanged; validity **poisoned** vs LKG positive. |\n| **T0 + 48h00m00s** | 172800s >= 172800 | true | Drops non-root members from `validity_map`; `_shrink_allowed` passes; **publishes a shrunk universe** even though the chain read never succeeded. |\n| **T0 + 49h** | >= 48h | true | Same removal logic; if 48h run already shrank, snapshot stays shrunk; no restoration on failed read. |\n\n## Blocking\n**poisons-later-row:** Failed/incomplete chain reads write `negative_since` and `validity=negative` for members that should stay last-good; cycle 2 at 48h reads that state back and removes them while the read is still failing.\n\n## Severity\nP0 — membership shrink on timeout/failure without a complete chain observation.\n\nRevert to `probe_val = None` when `not probe_complete and netuid not in probe_map`, or gate `False` only when `probe_complete` is true (aligned with `_merge_sources` “failed chain read does not undo an earlier chain verdict” ~219–221).",
