            "body": "## Summary\n\nPR 9101 replaces `(now - started).total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` with `elapsed.seconds >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` in `_eligible_for_removal`. **Measured** from head `internal/subnet_universe.py`: `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS = 172800` (48h). Python’s `timedelta.seconds` is only the sub-day component in `[0, 86399]`; it never includes whole days. Because `172800 > 86399`, the new predicate is **always false** — no elapsed time satisfies it.\n\n**Inferred** consumer path: `_shrink_allowed` calls `_eligible_for_removal` for each netuid dropped from the prior snapshot; when it stays false, shrink is blocked and deregistered netuids never age out of membership on grace alone.\n\n## Concrete elapsed times (deregistered subnet, probe false, `negative_since` set)\n\nAssume `elapsed = now - started`. Compare old (`total_seconds() >= 172800`) vs new (`elapsed.seconds >= 172800`).\n\n| Elapsed | `days` | `seconds` (component) | `total_seconds()` | Old eligible? | New eligible? |\n|--------|--------|-------------------------|---------------------|---------------|---------------|\n| **23h59m** (86340s) | 0 | 86340 | 86340 | No | No |\n| **24h00m** (86400s) | 1 | 0 | 86400 | No | No |\n| **24h01m** (86460s) | 1 | 60 | 86460 | No | No |\n| **47h59m** (172740s) | 1 | 86340 | 172740 | No | No |\n| **48h00m** (172800s) | 2 | 0 | 172800 | **Yes** | **No** |\n| **48h01m** (172861s) | 2 | 61 | 172861 | **Yes** | **No** |\n\nBoth sides of **24h**: still not eligible under either version (grace is 48h). The regression appears at **48h**: base correctly flips to eligible; head never does.\n\nAfter **48h**, old code stays eligible; new code stays ineligible forever (P1 **never-expires** for grace-based removal).\n\n## Fix direction\n\nRevert to `total_seconds()` (or compare `elapsed >= timedelta(seconds=STALE_GRACE_SECONDS)`), and add a test that `_eligible_for_removal` is true at exactly 48h elapsed.\n\n## Severities\n\n- **P1**: Grace-based removal never fires (`never-expires`).",
