      "finalText": "## Verdict: **FAIL** (posted on head `10bfa73cdbee1025a1466d6247d879ebe3d6b56e`)\n\n**Measured:** `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS = 172800` (48h). The diff swaps `total_seconds()` for `elapsed.seconds` on the same threshold.\n\n**Inferred:** `_eligible_for_removal` gates `_shrink_allowed`; if grace never passes, deregistered netuids do not shrink out on stale evidence alone (**never-expires**).\n\n### What the comparison does at concrete elapsed times\n\nFor a deregistered subnet (probe false, valid `negative_since`), eligibility is that one comparison. Python stores duration as whole **days** plus **seconds** in `[0, 86399]` only — not total span in `seconds`.\n\n| Elapsed | Old: `total_seconds() >= 172800` | New: `elapsed.seconds >= 172800` |\n|--------|-----------------------------------|-----------------------------------|\n| **23h59m** | No (86340) | No (86340; `days=0`) |\n| **24h00m** | No (86400) | No (`seconds=0`, `days=1`) |\n| **24h01m** | No (86460) | No (`seconds=60`, `days=1`) |\n| **47h59m** | No (172740) | No (`seconds=86340`, `days=1`) |\n| **48h00m** | **Yes** (172800) | **No** (`seconds=0`, `days=2`) |\n| **48h01m** | **Yes** (172861) | **No** (`seconds=61`, `days=2`) |\n\nAround **24h**, both versions stay ineligible (grace is 48h). The break is at **48h**: base flips to eligible; head **never** does, because `172800 > 86399` so `elapsed.seconds >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` is always false.\n\n**Fix:** use `total_seconds()` or compare to a `timedelta(seconds=STALE_GRACE_SECONDS)`; add a test at exactly 48h elapsed.",
