      "finalText": "## Verdict\n\n**FAIL** — `post_verdict` returned `posted: false, reason: eval` on every attempt at head `1748ed870dbd1a1e086dc3a611d6528596734001`, so the gate still shows **mc: missing** and **next: review**. The review below is what I attempted to post.\n\n### Measured\n\n- **Diff** on `internal/subnet_universe.py` removes the branch where `probe_positive is False` and `tmc_positive is not False` returned `\"negative\"`, set `negative_since`, and treated TMC listing as disputed (`tmc_positive is True`).\n- **Diff** adds a branch where `tmc_positive is True` and `probe_positive is False` returns `\"positive\"`, `disputed=True`, and `negative_since=None` (comment: treat disagreement as dispute, not removal).\n- **Head** `_default_probe_fetch` documents that per-netuid `False` is only produced after a successful pinned read (`outcome == \"ok\"`) — i.e. a **complete** membership map, not a failed/timeout read.\n- **Head** `_eligible_for_removal` requires `evidence.probe is False`, a set `negative_since`, and `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` (48h) before a netuid can drop.\n\n### Inferred\n\n- When TaoMarketCap lists a netuid and a **complete** probe says it is **not** on chain, validity stays **positive** and the removal clock is cleared. That contradicts the pinned contract: **a definitive chain negative beats a TaoMarketCap listing**.\n- That path never reaches `validity == \"negative\"`, so grace-based removal does not run for this disagreement (**never-expires** / **poisons-later-row** relative to the prior chain-wins behavior).\n- For **complete** `probe_positive is False` with `tmc_positive is None`, the removed chain-wins branch no longer runs; control falls into the `None`/refresh-incomplete paths and can **retain prior positive** instead of starting `negative_since`. That is not “unknown chain” — probe was observed **False** (**inferred** regression vs the deleted branch).\n\n### Blocking (declared)\n\n- `poisons-later-row` — positive `validity_map` while probe evidence is false for the same cycle’s merge.\n- `never-expires` — no `negative_since` on the TMC-true / probe-false dispute path, so `_eligible_for_removal` never applies.\n\n### What would align with the pinned contract\n\nRestore chain-wins for **complete** `probe_positive is False` when TaoMarketCap is not also false (optional `disputed` when TMC lists it), without treating **probe None** / incomplete reads as a negative — the existing `probe_positive is None` / `refresh_incomplete` handling already reflects that second clause.\n\n---\n\n**Gate:** `check_gate_state` still reports **next: review** until a verdict is recorded successfully. If you want this FAIL on the PR, retry `post_verdict` from your side or say if there is a required body/eval format for this fixture session.",
