            "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR replaces the `_merge_sources` branch that treated a **complete** registration probe `False` (netuid absent from `NetworksAdded` at a pinned finalized head) as **`negative`** — with grace via `negative_since` — when TaoMarketCap was not explicitly negative. The new branch runs only when **`tmc_positive is True` and `probe_positive is False`**, returning **`positive`**, **`disputed=True`**, and **`negative_since=None`**.\n\nThat directly contradicts the **pinned membership contract for this review**: a definitive chain negative beats a TaoMarketCap listing. A failed/unknown chain read is still handled elsewhere (`probe_positive is None` paths); this finding is only the **complete probe False** case.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Definitive chain negative no longer beats TMC (policy + removal path)\n\n**Measured:** At head, `_merge_sources` returns `\"positive\"` for `tmc_positive is True and probe_positive is False` (diff hunk in `internal/subnet_universe.py`).\n\n**Measured:** Base at the same location returned `\"negative\"`, set `negative_since` when missing, and documented owner rule: chain wins when a complete read does not list the netuid.\n\n**Inferred:** Through `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_merge_sources`, a netuid with complete `probe_map[n]=False` and TMC present never gets `validity==\"negative\"`, so `_eligible_for_removal` never runs (`evidence.probe is not False` is false for removal, but validity must be negative first). The row **never enters the 48h removal clock** while TMC still lists it — **never-expires** relative to the agreed grace/removal model.\n\n### P1 — Regression: `probe False` + `tmc None` with complete probe\n\n**Measured:** Base handled **`probe_positive is False and tmc_positive is not False`** (includes `tmc_positive is None`) as **`negative`**.\n\n**Measured:** Head removes that branch entirely. For `probe_positive is False` and `tmc_positive is None`, control falls into the generic `tmc_positive is None or probe_positive is None` branch, which **retains prior validity** with `refresh_incomplete=True` instead of recording a new chain negative.\n\n**Inferred:** With `probe_complete=True` and a definitive `False` in `probe_map`, membership should mark **`negative`** per contract; head can keep a prior **`positive`** row indefinitely when TMC fetch is incomplete — **never-expires** and **poisons-later-row** (persisted `validity_map` consumed on later refreshes and by readers).\n\n### P2 — Downstream scoring expectation drift\n\n**Measured:** `load_membership_receipt` in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` builds `inactive_netuids` only from entries with `validity == \"negative\"`, and comments that chain-unregistered netuids leave **expected** immediately (while row may remain for grace).\n\n**Inferred:** Disputed **`positive`** entries for `probe False` stay in **`expected_netuids`**, so phase-1 coverage/scoring denominators can **expect subnets the chain says are unregistered** — bad state later cycles read from the shared snapshot (**poisons-later-row**).\n\n## What still looks correct\n\n**Measured:** Branches for `probe_positive is None` while prior validity is `negative` still preserve the prior chain verdict without restarting grace — consistent with “unknown/failed chain read is NOT a negative.”\n\n**Measured:** `tmc False` + `probe False` still returns `negative` with `negative_since`.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nThe change is intentional per PR title, but it violates the pinned contract and removes coverage for the broader `probe False` / non-`tmc False` case. Restore chain-wins for **complete** `probe_positive is False` (dispute flag optional, but validity must be `negative` with grace), or narrow the PR and prove downstream receipts/tests align with dispute-as-positive.",
