      "finalText": "**FAIL** posted on [PR 9103](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9103) at `1748ed870dbd1a1e086dc3a611d6528596734001`.\n\nThe diff swaps out the base behavior where a **complete** registration probe `False` (`probe_positive is False`, netuid not in `NetworksAdded`) forced **`negative`** with `negative_since` whenever TMC was not explicitly `False` — including the documented “chain wins” owner rule. At head, **`tmc_positive is True` and `probe_positive is False`** yields **`positive`**, **`disputed=True`**, and **`negative_since=None`**, which conflicts with the pinned contract that a **definitive chain negative beats a TMC listing**.\n\n**Blocking findings**\n\n1. **Removal / grace never starts** for TMC-listed + chain-not-registered subnets: they no longer get `validity==\"negative\"`, so the 48h removal path in `_compute_membership` / `_eligible_for_removal` does not apply (**never-expires** in the grace model).\n\n2. **Regression for `probe False` + `tmc None`**: base treated that as negative via `tmc_positive is not False`; head drops that branch and can **keep prior `positive`** under the incomplete refresh path even when the probe was complete (**never-expires**, **poisons-later-row** via persisted `validity_map`).\n\n3. **Downstream**: `load_membership_receipt` only treats `validity==\"negative\"` as inactive for **expected** scoring set; disputed **positive** rows with `probe False` stay in **expected_netuids**, diverging from the chain-unregistered semantics still described in `snapshot_coverage.py` (**poisons-later-row**).\n\n**Unchanged (good):** failed/unknown probe (`probe_positive is None`) still does not undo a prior chain negative; `tmc False` + `probe False` still goes negative.\n\nTo move forward: restore chain-wins for **complete** `probe_positive is False` (negative + grace; dispute can be metadata), or shrink the change and align receipts/tests with “dispute keeps membership.”",
