          "toolName": "post_verdict",
          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe change adds diagnostic context on `_default_tmc_fetch` failure by building `tmc_env` from every `os.environ` entry whose name starts with `TMC` or `TAOMARKETCAP`, then passing that dict to `logger.warning` as `(config: %s)`.\n\n**measured:** At head, the except branch is:\n\n```python\ntmc_env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k.upper().startswith((\"TMC\", \"TAOMARKETCAP\"))}\nlogger.warning(\"subnet_universe TMC fetch failed: %s (config: %s)\", exc, tmc_env)\n```\n\n**measured:** The author’s staging log for an upstream 502 shows the warning includes a `config` mapping with `TMC_API_KEY` and its **full secret value**. That is exactly what this diff produces: values are copied verbatim from the environment into application logs (and any log shipper downstream).\n\n**inferred:** On failure, control flow is unchanged — still `return set(), {}, False` — so membership does not gain a new numeric overflow or grace-clock bug from this hunk. The regression is **credential disclosure**, not universe math.\n\n## Findings\n\n| ID | Severity | Label | Finding |\n|----|----------|-------|---------|\n| F1 | **P0** | measured | Logging raw `TMC*` / `TAOMARKETCAP*` env **values** on the failure path writes API keys and tokens into staging/production log stores. The pasted staging line confirms `TMC_API_KEY` is emitted in clear text. |\n| F2 | **P2** | inferred | Even non-secret vars (base URLs, feature flags) in the same dict increase leak blast radius when logs are shared for incident response — as in this PR thread. |\n\n## Required direction\n\nDo **not** log secret values. Acceptable patterns: log **key names only** (`sorted(tmc_env)` → list of names), or log `{k: (\"set\" if v else \"unset\") for k, v in ...}` without printing `v`, or reuse an existing repo redaction helper if one exists for TMC config.\n\nOperational note (not a gate merge action): any key that appeared in staging logs or this PR should be treated as compromised and rotated outside this review.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced failure path from `_default_tmc_fetch` through warning logger; confirmed no change to return tuple or membership merge on TMC incomplete | — |\n| owner-rules | Secret values must not appear in logs or review output; this diff violates that standing expectation | — |\n| settled-check | No need to re-litigate whether failed TMC should mark `tmc_complete=False` (unchanged); secret logging is not a settled “log the whole env” decision | — |\n\n502 from upstream is an operational incident; this PR does not fix that, and as written makes incident debugging **less** safe.",
