ycle 2 at each pinned time (changed code, probe still failing)\n\nEach row is one `build(prior)` with `now` at the pinned instant; prior is the snapshot produced by cycle 1 (or the prior cycle-2 build when times are sequential).\n\n| Build time | `now - negative_since` vs 48h | **Inferred** membership outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| **T0 + 47h59m59s** | **172799s** — **measured** `< 172800` | Members **remain** in `netuids`. Rows stay **negative** with the T0 `negative_since`; `_eligible_for_removal` is false, so nothing enters `dropped`. `refresh_incomplete` stays true. Universe **size matches LKG** but for the **wrong reason** (grace running on synthetic probe-false), not “nothing observed”. |\n| **T0 + 48h00m00s** | **172800s** — **measured** `>= 172800` | Non-root members with that `negative_since` become **`dropped`**, drop out of `validity_map`, and **`netuids` shrinks**. If `_shrink_allowed` passes (probe evidence `False`), `refresh_once` **publishes the smaller universe**. |\n| **T0 + 49h** | **≥ 172800** | **Inferred:** Same shrunk universe as at 48h; removed netuids stay out. No contract (2) retention. |\n\n**Under pinned contract (2)** (no clock on failed read), all three cycle-2 times would **retain LKG membership and prior validity** — behavior that **`probe_val=None`** on incomplete absence from `probe_map` preserved via the `probe_positive is None` branches in `_merge_sources`.\n\n## Blocking finding\n\n**poisons-later-row (P0):** Treating “absent from `probe_map` while `probe_complete` is false” as **`probe_val=False`** on a **total** probe failure equates “read failed” with “chain says not registered”, seeds `negative_since` on cycle 1, and **removes members at the 48h boundary** on cycle 2 even though the chain never successfully reported registration — the opposite of contract (2).\n\n## Verdict\n\n**FAIL** — one-line hunk is inconsistent with the module’s own observation contract and causes deregistration clocks on failed reads.",
