            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe one-line behavior change in `_compute_membership` treats a missing probe entry under an **incomplete** chain read as `probe_val = False`. That value is consumed by `_merge_sources` as if the chain had reported “not registered,” which starts or preserves a `negative_since` clock and can drop members after 48h even though `_default_probe_fetch` documents that a failed read observes nothing.\n\nThis conflicts with the pinned membership contract (failed/timeout chain read → retain last-good membership and validity; no deregistration clock).\n\n## Diff (measured)\n\nAt head `7b1b568539ffbaaf49ccc7a4d14ff1bcceff79c5`, `internal/subnet_universe.py` changes the branch `if not probe_complete and netuid not in probe_map` from `probe_val = None` to `probe_val = False` (with comment). **Measured** via `get_pr_diff`.\n\n## Consumption trace (measured)\n\n1. Failed chain read: `_default_probe_fetch` returns `({}, False)` when pin/read fails or times out (**measured** in `subnet_universe.py`).\n2. For each prior member `netuid` not in the empty `probe_map`, the changed code sets `probe_val = False` while `probe_complete` remains `False` (**measured**).\n3. `_merge_sources(..., tmc_positive=True, probe_positive=False)` hits the early branch “Owner rule: the chain wins…” and, if `negative_since` is empty, sets `negative_since = _now_iso()` and `validity = \"negative\"` (**measured**). This branch does **not** require `probe_complete`.\n4. Removal requires `_eligible_for_removal`: `evidence.probe is not False` must be false (i.e. probe exactly `False`), plus `negative_since` set, plus `(now - started).total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` where `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS = 172800` and the comparison is `>=` (**measured**).\n5. With the **prior** code (`probe_val = None`), the same incomplete probe yields `tmc_positive is True or probe_positive is True` → `positive` with `negative_since = None`, and `_eligible_for_removal` fails on `evidence.probe is not False` because probe stays `None` (**measured**).\n\n## Pinned scenario — cycle 2 at three times (inferred)\n\nAssume: last-good universe from a prior **complete** successful chain read; cycle 1 at `T0` and cycle 2 each run with chain read still failing (`probe_map = {}`, `probe_complete = False`); TaoMarketCap complete so `tmc_positive=True` for registered members; grace 48h, check `>=`.\n\n**Inferred** from measured merge/eligibility rules after cycle 1 at `T0` has already written `negative_since = T0` and `probe=False` for those members:\n\n| Cycle 2 time | What the changed code does |\n|---|---|\n| `T0 + 47h59m59s` | Elapsed `172799s < 172800` → not eligible for removal. Members **remain in** `validity_map` / `netuids`; `negative_since` stays `T0`; validity stays **negative** (already poisoned at cycle 1). |\n| `T0 + 48h00m00s` | Elapsed `172800s >= 172800` → **eligible**. Members are **dropped** from membership (`dropped[netuid]`, shrink) even though no successful chain read occurred at either cycle. |\n| `T0 + 49h` | If the `48h00m00s` run already dropped them, they **stay out**. If only this timestamp ran after cycle 1, `negative_since` would still be `T0` and `49h` elapsed would also satisfy grace → drop (**inferred**). |\n\nUnder the pinned contract, all three times should **retain** last-good membership and **not** advance a deregistration clock; the changed code instead starts the clock at cycle 1 and removes at the `>= 48h` boundary.\n\n## Finding (blocking)\n\n**P1 — Incomplete probe synthesized as chain negative (`poisons-later-row`)**  \n**Measured:** assignment `probe_val = False` when `not probe_complete`. **Inferred:** drives `_merge_sources` chain-win path and `_eligible_for_removal` with `probe=False`, contradicting `_default_probe_fetch` docstring (“nothing is observed… keeps prior members”) and the pinned fail/timeout contract.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**FAIL** — do not merge until missing probe entries under `probe_complete=False` remain unobserved (`None`) or `_merge_sources` refuses to treat `probe_positive=False` as a complete chain verdict unless `probe_complete` is true.",
