      "finalText": "I'm **subnet-review-gate**. MC verdict for PR 9306 at head `7b1b568539ffbaaf49ccc7a4d14ff1bcceff79c5`: **FAIL** (formal `post_verdict` returned `posted: false` in this fixture session; content below is the review body).\n\n## What changed (measured)\n\nIn `_compute_membership`, when `not probe_complete` and `netuid not in probe_map`, the diff replaces `probe_val = None` with `probe_val = False` (`get_pr_diff`).\n\nOn a failed chain read, `_default_probe_fetch` returns `({}, False)` (**measured**). Prior members are absent from `probe_map`, so the new branch sets **`probe_val = False`** while **`probe_complete` stays False**.\n\n## Why that breaks the pinned contract (measured → inferred)\n\n`_merge_sources` treats `probe_positive is False` with `tmc_positive is not False` as the “chain wins” path: it sets `validity = \"negative\"` and, if empty, **`negative_since = _now_iso()`** — with **no** check that `probe_complete` is true (**measured**).\n\nThat contradicts contract (2): a failed/timeout read should observe nothing, keep last-good validity, and **not** start a deregistration clock. The fetch docstring says the same: nothing observed, prior members kept (**measured**).\n\nWith the old `None` assignment, `tmc_positive is True` and `probe_positive is None` yield **positive** and **`negative_since = None`**, and `_eligible_for_removal` rejects removal because `evidence.probe is not False` when probe is `None` (**measured**).\n\n**Blocking:** `poisons-later-row` — incomplete probe is written as chain-negative and schedules later drops.\n\n## Cycle 2 at the three pinned times (changed code)\n\nAssume: last-good universe from an earlier **complete** chain read; cycle **1** at **T0** already ran with probe still failing (`probe_map = {}`, `probe_complete = False`) and TMC complete (`tmc_positive = True` for members). Cycle **1** therefore already set **`negative_since = T0`** and **`probe = False`** for those members (**inferred** from measured merge rules).\n\n| Time | Behavior under changed code |\n|------|-------------------------------|\n| **T0 + 47h59m59s** | Elapsed **172799s**; grace is **`>= 172800`** → **not** eligible. Members **stay in** the universe; **`negative_since` remains T0**; validity stays **negative** (poisoned at cycle 1). |\n| **T0 + 48h00m00s** | Elapsed **172800s** → **eligible**. Members are **dropped** from membership even though **no** successful chain read ran in cycle 1 or 2. |\n| **T0 + 49h** | After the 48h drop, they **remain out** (**inferred**). |\n\nUnder the **pinned contract**, all three cycle-2 runs should **retain** last-good membership and **not** run a deregistration clock; the changed code instead starts the clock at cycle 1 and removes at the **`>= 48h`** boundary.\n\n## Fix direction (inferred)\n\nKeep **`probe_val = None`** when `not probe_complete`, **or** gate the chain-win branch in `_merge_sources` so `probe_positive is False` only applies when **`probe_complete` is true**.\n\nGate `next` remains **`review`** in this fixture (`mc` still **missing**). After a real `post_verdict`, the gate moves to **`await_cursor_ditto`** per `lib/gate.ts`.",
