d:** If shrink published at 48h, membership stays at the reduced set; continued failed reads keep treating unmapped netuids as `probe_val=False`, so removed netuids do not re-enter without positive observation. |\n\n**Verdict:** **FAIL** — incomplete chain read must not synthesize `probe=False` (chain verdict). That starts a deregistration clock and evicts members after 48h despite never observing registration status on those cycles, contradicting the pinned membership contract and the module's own failed-read semantics.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Failed incomplete probe traced through `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_merge_sources` → `_eligible_for_removal` / `_shrink_allowed`; missing map entry becomes chain-negative | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins on **complete** read is documented in `_merge_sources`; this diff applies chain-negative on **incomplete** read | — |\n| settled-check | Prior `probe_val=None` path retained prior validity without starting `negative_since` on probe miss (measured base diff) | — |",
