      "finalText": "**FAIL** posted on head `7b1b568539ffbaaf49ccc7a4d14ff1bcceff79c5`.\n\nThe diff sets `probe_val = False` when the chain read is incomplete and a netuid is absent from `probe_map`. That is **not** “nothing observed.” **Measured:** `_merge_sources` treats `probe_positive is False` with `tmc_positive is not False` (including `None`) as a chain verdict, sets `validity=\"negative\"`, and stamps `negative_since` at cycle time. **Inferred:** that contradicts your pinned contract and `_default_probe_fetch`’s failed-read semantics (`probe_val=None` on base kept prior validity without starting a clock).\n\n### Cycle 2 with the changed code (chain still failing)\n\nAssume cycle 1 at **T0** already ran with the new line, so prior rows carry `negative_since = T0` and `probe=False` evidence on each refresh.\n\n| Time | What cycle 2 does |\n| --- | --- |\n| **T0 + 47h59m59s** | Grace not met (`>= 172800` is false at 172799s). Members stay in the universe; validity stays `negative` with clock anchored at T0; refresh stays incomplete/degraded. |\n| **T0 + 48h00m00s** | Grace met at exactly 48h. `_eligible_for_removal` passes (`probe is False`, `negative_since` set). Netuids drop out of `validity_map`; the universe **shrinks** when `_shrink_allowed` accepts the drops. |\n| **T0 + 49h** | If shrink published at 48h, membership remains reduced; further failed reads keep treating missing probe keys as `False`, so removed netuids do not return without a positive observation. |\n\n**Blocking:** `poisons-later-row` — a failed read writes `negative_since` and later cycles evict on grace even though the chain never successfully reported deregistration on those cycles.",
