          "toolName": "post_verdict",
          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nTwo-file change: adds `_cycle_complete(coverage) -> bool` as `bool(coverage.get(\"complete\"))` and routes `note_cycle` through it; adds `test_cycle_complete_reads_coverage_flag` for True/False.\n\n## Trace (inferred from diff + base `note_cycle`)\n\n**Measured:** `get_pr_diff` at `0a884e0e6823552bf9674b6da611443674adb3a2` shows only this extraction and call-site swap in `note_cycle`. Base `note_cycle` used `if coverage.get(\"complete\"):` (**measured** via `read_repo_file` at base).\n\n**Inferred:** For any value `v` returned by `coverage.get(\"complete\")`, `if v:` and `if bool(v):` agree on branch taken, so consecutive-partial streak reset/increment behavior is unchanged. Missing `complete` → `None` → partial increment, same as before.\n\n**Inferred:** `build_coverage_block` still sets top-level `\"complete\"` as a bool (**measured** in full module read); this PR does not alter that producer.\n\n## Edge values (inferred)\n\n`NaN`, `inf`, large ints, strings: same truthiness/`bool()` pairing as the prior inline check; no new path to overflow, stuck rows, or cross-cycle poisoned state — only a read of an existing flag.\n\n## Nits (non-blocking)\n\n- Extra blank lines before `_cycle_complete` in the patch (**measured**).\n- Test does not assert missing-key/`None`/`0`; optional given unchanged semantics.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nNo finding in the never-expires / overflow / aborts-cycle / poisons-later-row classes. Refactor + unit test only.",
