            "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds `queries_for_refresh` (ceiling division for refresh batch count) and a single test `64 / batch_size 32 → 2`. Math for positive `netuid_count` and positive `batch_size` is **inferred** correct from the formula `(netuid_count + batch_size - 1) // batch_size`; `netuid_count <= 0` returns `0` (**measured** from `read_repo_file` at head).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — `batch_size=0` aborts the call (blocking: aborts-cycle)\n\n**Inferred:** With `batch_size=0`, the return line executes integer division by zero and raises `ZeroDivisionError`. There is no guard; the public keyword-only `batch_size` is not clamped. Elsewhere in this repo’s internal config seams, sizes are bounded with patterns like `max(1, env_int(...))` (**measured** in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` at head). When this helper is wired into refresh batch planning, a misconfigured or computed zero batch size would abort that refresh path rather than returning a safe count.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Clamp `batch_size = max(1, batch_size)` (or reject `batch_size < 1` explicitly) and add a unit test for `batch_size=0` / `batch_size=1` and a partial final batch (e.g. `netuid_count=33`, `batch_size=32` → `2`).\n\n### P3 — No production consumer in this PR\n\n**Measured:** `list_repo_files` at head shows no import of `r1b_perf_08` outside the new test file. Acceptable if this is an incremental R1B perf scaffold; title implies future wiring.\n\n### P3 — Test surface is minimal\n\n**Measured:** Only `queries_for_refresh(64, batch_size=32) == 2` is asserted. Edge cases (`0`, `1`, remainder batch) are untested.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `netuid_count` and `batch_size` through `queries_for_refresh`; `batch_size=0` → division by zero (**inferred**) | none |\n| owner-rules | Config sizing elsewhere uses `max(1, …)` (**measured** pattern in snapshot_coverage) | none |\n| settled-check | No roadmap/doc in fixture tree for R1B-08; not re-litigating | none |\n\nNo float/`inf` paths in this helper; no row persistence.",
