            "body": "## Scope\n\nPR extracts `probe_candidates = sorted(candidates)` in `SnapshotBuilder.build` (when `tmc_complete`) into `_sorted_probe_candidates(candidates: set[int]) -> list[int]` returning `sorted(candidates)`, plus a unit test.\n\n## Entry point trace\n\n**Measured:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` still builds `candidates` as `set(tmc_positive) | prior_members | range(MAX_NETUIDS)` when TMC is complete, then passes the resulting list to `self._probe_fetch` or `_default_probe_fetch` (`internal/subnet_universe.py` at head, `build` around the `probe_candidates` assignment).\n\n**Measured:** `_default_probe_fetch` maps every requested netuid (except `ROOT_NETUID`) against the chain registration set and merges in any registered netuids missing from the list; list order does not change which keys appear in `probe_map` when the read completes.\n\n**Inferred:** Replacing inline `sorted(candidates)` with `_sorted_probe_candidates(candidates)` yields the same ascending int order as before, because the helper is a direct `sorted()` on the same `set[int]` built at the call site. No new inputs (no floats, NaN, strings, or unbounded magnitudes) enter this path.\n\n## Adversarial checks (owner hot values)\n\n**Inferred:** `1e308`, denormals, `10**400`, `2**63`, NaN/inf, and bool-as-number paths are not introduced; candidates remain bounded netuid ints capped by `MAX_NETUIDS = 200`. **Inferred:** No change to 48h grace (`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`), chain-wins merge logic, or refresh incompleteness handling in `_compute_membership` / `_merge_sources`.\n\n## Test\n\n**Measured:** `test_sorted_probe_candidates_orders_netuids` asserts `{3,1,2} -> [1,2,3]` on the helper. **Inferred:** This locks sort semantics only; it does not alter production behavior beyond the refactor.\n\n## Findings\n\nNone. Refactor-only; no never-expire, overflow, cycle-abort, or cross-row poison paths identified.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nTried to break membership or probe semantics via ordering and extreme-value framing; the change is naming/indirection over existing `sorted(set[int])` behavior at the real `build` → probe_fetch entry point.",
